{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>My sabbaths you shall keep.</b> The warnings concerning the Sabbath are numerous in the Torah, just as with idolatry, because it too is weighted equally against all the commandments, for one who does not keep it denies the act of Creation and has no Torah at all. And according to our Rabbis there is a midrash concerning it, for they said here: It might be thought that the building of the Temple overrides the Sabbath — Scripture teaches: \"My sabbaths you shall keep, and My sanctuary you shall revere, I am YHWH,\" in Torat Kohanan (chapter 7:6). And by way of truth, He commands concerning the great Sabbath and concerning the Sabbath which is His sanctuary, and He commands regarding it keeping and reverence, and behold, the labors of the Temple do not override the Sabbath and the Sanctuary. And if you will understand, you will comprehend."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:56:41.610884002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}